Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 05:19:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] CUDA: TQ1_0 / TQ2_0 MMQ through the Q8_0 kernels (codes
 unpacked to int8 {-1, 0, 1} in the tile)

One scale per 256 values needs no per-16 rescaling: the Q8_0 tensor-core path instead of Q2_K's. Prefill (pp512,
RTX 4080 Laptop): 27B TTF TQ2_0 450 -> 630 tok/s, TQ1_0 390 -> 512; 0.8B TQ2_0 9.0k -> 12.9k (bf16 13.7k).
test-backend-ops MUL_MAT: 0 failures. TQ1_0 and TQ2_0 give the same NLL (same trits): 0.8B 2.589127.
